Well, my Barbarian finally made it out.  I was level 26 with 315 h.p., +2
GDSM, +7 Vorpal Blade.  Went through 2 amulets of Life Saving, and was
about to use up my 3rd when I made it.  (I was sick.)

I attained a -26 AC twice, but lost it twice also after killing friendlies
(accidentally).  I also had my blindfold cursed while it was on, not once,
not twice, but THREE TIMES.  I took to carrying two with me at all times.
I also would have been much tougher had I not lost levels to Wraiths and
Vampires after being frozen by Shades.  Man, those dudes are tough.  I
will definitely use Excalibur only from now on.  

I NEVER saw a single potion of holy water or a lawful altar.  I had to
wish for all of my good stuff.  All of the shops were full of junk.  Had
to kill my own Archon, but polymorphed him first because he was kicking
my butt.

Here are my gripes:

The end game is lame.  Especially floating around on the water level.  I
don't think it's fun to search every square for the portal.  I also didn't
enjoy being zapped back levels after I had acquired the amulet, but I 
guess that's part of the game.

It's not clear as to what you're supposed to do on the very last level.
The bell-book-candle thing should be more clearly defined.  I asked the
Oracle, but what it told me was pretty vague.

As for the bug: The Amulet was lost because the High Priest was turned to
stone by a cockatrice.  Luckily I had a backup of my save file (to use
only in extremely unfair cases like this one).  If something is turned to
stone, it ought to drop its stuff.  Especially something like this.

Also, could somebody tell me what caused the random cursings of my items,
and the sudden appearance of monsters around me?  I think it was probably
the Book of the Dead, but I'm not sure.

Otherwise, I thought it was pretty easy.  Once you're tough enough to
take on a certain level of monster you can stay alive through the whole
game.  Also, I found that drinking all of those healing/extra healing
potions along the way must have gained me at least 50 extra hit points.

It took me forever, but I'm finally through it.  Guess I can go back to
my life now...

